<div id="2026-11-12-schema-compare-table-flags" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-12 — Schema-compare tables list: flag real Result-vs-live drift</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The tables list showed every matched table as fine. Real column, key, and missing-side drift was only visible after opening a single table, and earlier field comparison still treated some equivalent values (int vs int(11), display widths, NULL vs no default, name case, unsigned/charset noise, Result varchar default size 255, enum lists) as problems.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> Comparison now lives in <code>Comserv::Util::Schema::Equivalence</code> (the controller keeps thin wrappers so existing tests still call <code>_fields_equivalent</code>). <code>Inspector</code> fetches one information_schema catalog of columns and keys before the connection is closed. <code>schema_compare_database</code> runs <code>compare_table</code> for every table, stashes an issue count, and the tables list shows a Status badge, issue details, a flagged-table count, and a “Problems only” filter. Equivalent values are not flagged; extra live indexes the Result file never declared are ignored. Result files and the live database are not changed.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Schema/Equivalence.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Schema/Inspector.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/Schema/ResultParser.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/SchemaComparison.pm</code>, <code>root/admin/schema_compare/tables.tt</code>, <code>root/static/js/schema-compare.js</code>, <code>root/static/css/themes/schema_compare.css</code>, <code>t/schema_comparison_field_equivalence.t</code>, <code>t/schema_table_diff.t</code>, this changelog fragment.</p>
</div>
